---
// concept: An engineering drawing sheet — a full-width masthead over three hairline "notes" columns, closed by an edge-to-edge blueprint plate: the plan view of the AWS architecture one command generates, with a title block, a dimension line and a pending revision stamp along its foot.
// copy-angle: Lead on depth rather than convenience — "AWS DevOps, fully automated. Down to the subnet." — and play the AI claim as reviewable engineering rather than autonomy: the agent files the fix as a revision you sign off, and letting it sign for itself is a setting that ships off.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Logo from '../../components/Logo.astro';
import { CtaCommand } from '../../components/CtaCommand';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Stacktape — AWS DevOps, fully automated"
  description="One config file becomes production-grade AWS infrastructure in your own account: VPCs, private subnets, TLS, autoscaling, least-privilege IAM, pipelines, metrics, traces, alarms and incident response — generated from your repository and operated for you."
  font="geist"
  noindex
>
  <div class="hc3">
    <header class="nav">
      <div class="wrap nav__inner">
        <a class="nav__brand" href="/" aria-label="Stacktape home"><Logo height={22} /></a>
        <nav class="nav__links" aria-label="Primary">
          <a href="https://docs.stacktape.com">Docs</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/stacktape/stacktape">GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://cal.com/stacktape/30min">Book a demo</a>
        </nav>
        <a class="nav__cta" href="https://console.stacktape.com/sign-up">Sign up</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="masthead">
          <div class="masthead__top">
            <p class="eyebrow">One config file · Your AWS account · The entire job</p>
            <p class="strapline">
              For teams with developers and no DevOps department — and for the platform teams who would rather review
              the drawing than draw it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <h1 class="title">
            <span class="l1">AWS DevOps, fully automated.</span>
            <span class="l2">Down to the subnet.</span>
          </h1>
        </div>

        <section class="notes" aria-label="What Stacktape does">
          <div class="note">
            <p class="note__label"><span class="note__num">Note 01</span> The job</p>
            <p class="note__body">
              <code>npx stacktape init</code> reads your repository on your machine and writes one config file. One
              deploy compiles it to plain CloudFormation and builds the architecture drawn below in your own AWS account
              — VPC, private subnets, TLS, autoscaling, least-privilege IAM.
            </p>
            <p class="note__body">
              The first deploy is the smaller half. Pipelines, metrics, traces, logs, alarms, budgets and incident
              response are attached to the same stack from the start, and stay attached for as long as it runs.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="note">
            <p class="note__label"><span class="note__num">Note 02</span> What it does not skip</p>
            <ul class="depth">
              <li>
                <span class="depth__k">Networking</span>
                <span class="depth__v"
                >Multi-AZ VPCs, private-only services, NAT egress, bastion access, GPU and Spot workloads.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="depth__k">Governance</span>
                <span class="depth__v"
                >Roles and permissions, budgets, audit trails and 18 guardrail types, enforced per stage.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="depth__k">No lock-in</span>
                <span class="depth__v"
                >Plain CloudFormation out. Drop a CDK construct or raw CloudFormation in anywhere. Cancel Stacktape and
                  the stack keeps running.</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="depth__k">Already on AWS</span>
                <span class="depth__v"
                >It reads Docker Compose, Dockerfiles, Procfiles, Serverless, SAM, SST, CDK and Terraform, so it starts
                  from what you have.</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="note note--cta">
            <p class="note__label"><span class="note__num">Note 03</span> Start</p>
            <div class="cta-slot">
              <CtaCommand client:visible defaultMethod="npx" />
            </div>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn--solid" href="https://console.stacktape.com/sign-up">
                Deploy in the Console
                <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="13" height="13" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path
                    d="M3 8h9M8.5 4.5 12 8l-3.5 3.5"
                    fill="none"
                    stroke="currentColor"
                    stroke-width="1.5"
                    stroke-linecap="round"
                    stroke-linejoin="round"
                  >
                  </path>
                </svg>
              </a>
              <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="https://cal.com/stacktape/30min">Book a demo</a>
            </div>
            <p class="fine">
              The CLI and the framework are open source. The wizard runs on your machine, sends no code to Stacktape and
              creates nothing on AWS — it writes one file.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <figure class="plate">
          <figcaption class="plate__head">
            <span>Plan view — acme-project / production</span>
            <span class="plate__head-r">Generated from stacktape.yml · not drawn by hand</span>
          </figcaption>

          <div class="plate__canvas">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 1440 404"
              role="img"
              aria-label="Plan view of the AWS architecture generated from one Stacktape config: a WAF and CDN at the edge, an application load balancer and NAT gateways in public subnets, Fargate services and a Lambda worker in private application subnets across two availability zones, Aurora PostgreSQL with a failover reader and a Redis cache in private data subnets, and metrics, traces, logs, alarms and incidents wired alongside."
            >
              <defs>
                <marker
                  id="hc3-arw"
                  viewBox="0 0 8 8"
                  refX="7.2"
                  refY="4"
                  markerWidth="6"
                  markerHeight="6"
                  orient="auto"
                >
                  <path d="M0 1 L7 4 L0 7 Z" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.34)"></path>
                </marker>
              </defs>

              <g class="layer-frame">
                <text class="bp-t" x="14" y="21">Your AWS account · eu-west-1 · your IAM, your bill</text>
                <text class="bp-t bp-end" x="1428" y="21">Plan view · sheet 1 of 1</text>
                <rect class="bp-acct" x="12" y="30" width="1416" height="362" rx="7"></rect>
                <rect class="bp-vpc" x="204" y="50" width="1024" height="316" rx="6"></rect>
                <rect class="bp-knock" x="216" y="42" width="152" height="16"></rect>
                <text class="bp-t bp-vpclabel" x="222" y="54">VPC · 10.0.0.0/16</text>
              </g>

              <g class="layer-bands">
                <rect class="bp-band" x="224" y="96" width="180" height="240" rx="5"></rect>
                <rect class="bp-band" x="428" y="96" width="360" height="240" rx="5"></rect>
                <rect class="bp-band" x="812" y="96" width="404" height="240" rx="5"></rect>
                <rect class="bp-band" x="1252" y="96" width="164" height="240" rx="5"></rect>
                <line class="bp-az-line" x1="210" y1="212" x2="1222" y2="212"></line>
                <text class="bp-col" x="32" y="88">Edge</text>
                <text class="bp-col" x="224" y="88">Public subnets</text>
                <text class="bp-col" x="428" y="88">Private subnets · application</text>
                <text class="bp-col" x="812" y="88">Private subnets · data</text>
                <text class="bp-col" x="1252" y="88">Observability</text>
                <text class="bp-az" transform="rotate(-90 214 152)" x="214" y="152">eu-west-1a</text>
                <text class="bp-az" transform="rotate(-90 214 282)" x="214" y="282">eu-west-1b</text>
              </g>

              <g class="layer-conn">
                <path class="bp-dash" d="M110 174 V250"></path>
                <text class="bp-note" x="118" y="216">attached</text>
                <path class="bp-line" d="M188 278 H210 V206 H232" marker-end="url(#hc3-arw)"></path>
                <path class="bp-line" d="M312 206 H416 V146 H436" marker-end="url(#hc3-arw)"></path>
                <path class="bp-line" d="M312 206 H416 V278 H436" marker-end="url(#hc3-arw)"></path>
                <path class="bp-line" d="M620 146 H820" marker-end="url(#hc3-arw)"></path>
                <path class="bp-line" d="M620 278 H632" marker-end="url(#hc3-arw)"></path>
                <path class="bp-line" d="M776 278 H820" marker-end="url(#hc3-arw)"></path>
                <path class="bp-line" d="M530 306 V322 H900 V310" marker-end="url(#hc3-arw)"></path>
                <path class="bp-line" d="M1000 278 H1020" marker-end="url(#hc3-arw)"></path>
                <path class="bp-dash" d="M1228 212 H1252"></path>
              </g>

              <g class="layer-node">
                <rect class="bp-n" x="32" y="118" width="156" height="56" rx="4"></rect>
                <text class="bp-nt" x="44" y="142">firewall</text>
                <text class="bp-ns" x="44" y="158">WAF · managed rules</text>

                <rect class="bp-n" x="32" y="250" width="156" height="56" rx="4"></rect>
                <text class="bp-nt" x="44" y="274">web</text>
                <text class="bp-ns" x="44" y="290">Next.js · CDN + server</text>

                <rect class="bp-n bp-n--edge" x="236" y="118" width="76" height="188" rx="4"></rect>
                <text class="bp-nt bp-mid" x="274" y="198">ALB</text>
                <text class="bp-ns bp-mid" x="274" y="214">TLS · ACM</text>

                <rect class="bp-n" x="324" y="118" width="72" height="56" rx="4"></rect>
                <text class="bp-nt bp-mid" x="360" y="142">NAT</text>
                <text class="bp-ns bp-mid" x="360" y="158">egress</text>

                <rect class="bp-n" x="324" y="250" width="72" height="56" rx="4"></rect>
                <text class="bp-nt bp-mid" x="360" y="274">NAT</text>
                <text class="bp-ns bp-mid" x="360" y="290">egress</text>

                <rect class="bp-n" x="440" y="118" width="180" height="56" rx="4"></rect>
                <text class="bp-nt" x="452" y="142">apiService</text>
                <text class="bp-ns" x="452" y="158">Fargate · 0.5 vCPU / 1 GB</text>

                <rect class="bp-n" x="440" y="250" width="180" height="56" rx="4"></rect>
                <text class="bp-nt" x="452" y="274">apiService</text>
                <text class="bp-ns" x="452" y="290">replica · other AZ</text>

                <rect class="bp-n" x="636" y="250" width="140" height="56" rx="4"></rect>
                <text class="bp-nt" x="648" y="274">worker</text>
                <text class="bp-ns" x="648" y="290">Lambda · jobs</text>

                <rect class="bp-n" x="824" y="118" width="176" height="56" rx="4"></rect>
                <text class="bp-nt" x="836" y="142">cache</text>
                <text class="bp-ns" x="836" y="158">Redis 7 · cache.t3.micro</text>

                <rect class="bp-n" x="824" y="250" width="176" height="56" rx="4"></rect>
                <text class="bp-nt" x="836" y="274">mainDatabase</text>
                <text class="bp-ns" x="836" y="290">Aurora PG 16.4 · writer</text>

                <rect class="bp-n" x="1024" y="250" width="176" height="56" rx="4"></rect>
                <text class="bp-nt" x="1036" y="274">mainDatabase</text>
                <text class="bp-ns" x="1036" y="290">reader · failover</text>
              </g>

              <g class="layer-anno">
                <text class="bp-note bp-mid" x="530" y="192">scale 2 → 6 tasks</text>
                <text class="bp-note bp-teal" x="1024" y="134">Private only</text>
                <text class="bp-note" x="1024" y="148">reachable from the application</text>
                <text class="bp-note" x="1024" y="162">subnets, and nowhere else</text>
                <text class="bp-note" x="1024" y="176">accessibilityMode: vpc</text>

                <line class="bp-dim" x1="210" y1="352" x2="1222" y2="352"></line>
                <line class="bp-dim" x1="210" y1="346" x2="210" y2="358"></line>
                <line class="bp-dim" x1="1222" y1="346" x2="1222" y2="358"></line>
                <rect class="bp-knock" x="502" y="344" width="428" height="16"></rect>
                <text class="bp-t bp-mid" x="716" y="356">
                  3 subnet tiers · 2 availability zones · no public IP on any workload
                </text>
              </g>

              <g class="layer-ops">
                <rect class="bp-ops" x="1266" y="110" width="136" height="26" rx="3"></rect>
                <text class="bp-ns bp-ops-t" x="1278" y="127">metrics</text>
                <rect class="bp-ops" x="1266" y="146" width="136" height="26" rx="3"></rect>
                <text class="bp-ns bp-ops-t" x="1278" y="163">traces</text>
                <rect class="bp-ops" x="1266" y="182" width="136" height="26" rx="3"></rect>
                <text class="bp-ns bp-ops-t" x="1278" y="199">logs</text>
                <rect class="bp-ops" x="1266" y="218" width="136" height="26" rx="3"></rect>
                <text class="bp-ns bp-ops-t" x="1278" y="235">alarms</text>
                <rect class="bp-ops bp-ops--hot" x="1266" y="254" width="136" height="26" rx="3"></rect>
                <line class="bp-tick" x1="1267" y1="256" x2="1267" y2="278"></line>
                <text class="bp-ns bp-ops-t bp-teal" x="1278" y="271">incidents</text>
                <text class="bp-note" x="1266" y="300">wired at deploy</text>
                <text class="bp-note" x="1266" y="314">no second vendor</text>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="rev">
            <p class="rev__stamp">Rev. 8 · prepared by the agent — awaiting sign-off</p>
            <p class="rev__text">
              When production breaks, the agent starts from this drawing: the config, the release diff, the traces, the
              logs and the account itself. It files the fix as a change you can read, and you sign it off. Letting it
              sign for itself is a setting, and it ships off.
            </p>
          </div>

          <dl class="tblock">
            <div>
              <dt>Declared</dt>
              <dd>6 resources in stacktape.yml</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Emitted</dt>
              <dd>33 CloudFormation resources</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Account</dt>
              <dd>Yours. AWS bills you directly, with no markup.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Pipeline</dt>
              <dd>EC2 runner in your account — typically 2–5× faster than CodeBuild.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Operations</dt>
              <dd>Metrics, traces, logs, alarms and costs on the same stack.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.hc3 {
  --ink: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.93);
  --ink-2: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.63);
  --ink-3: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
  --line: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  --line-2: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  --teal: var(--stp-color-brand);
  --teal-lit: color-mix(in srgb, var(--stp-color-brand) 84%, #eafffb);
  --cell: rgb(20, 25, 25);
  position: relative;
  isolation: isolate;
  overflow-x: clip;
}

.hc3::before {
  content: '';
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: -1;
  pointer-events: none;
  background:
    radial-gradient(880px 520px at 10% -8%, rgba(54, 190, 190, 0.11), transparent 62%),
    radial-gradient(720px 440px at 94% 2%, rgba(34, 87, 122, 0.16), transparent 66%),
    linear-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.016) 1px, transparent 1px) 0 0 / 64px 64px,
    linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.016) 1px, transparent 1px) 0 0 / 64px 64px;
  -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(180deg, #000 0%, #000 52%, transparent 96%);
  mask-image: linear-gradient(180deg, #000 0%, #000 52%, transparent 96%);
}

.wrap {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 1440px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 clamp(20px, 3vw, 48px);
}

.nav {
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2);
}

.nav__inner {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 28px;
  height: 66px;
}

.nav__brand {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
}

.nav__links {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 26px;
  margin-left: auto;
  font-size: 13.5px;
  color: var(--ink-2);
}

.nav__links a:hover {
  color: var(--ink);
}

.nav__cta {
  font-size: 13px;
  font-weight: 550;
  color: #08201f;
  background: var(--teal);
  border-radius: var(--stp-radius-medium);
  padding: 8px 15px;
  line-height: 1;
  transition: filter var(--stp-motion-duration-fast) var(--stp-motion-easing);
}

.nav__cta:hover {
  filter: brightness(1.08);
}

.hero {
  padding-bottom: clamp(40px, 7vh, 84px);
}

.masthead {
  padding-top: clamp(34px, 5.5vh, 66px);
}

.masthead__top {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 40px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.eyebrow {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 11px;
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--font-geist-mono);
  font-size: 10.5px;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.17em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-3);
}

.eyebrow::before {
  content: '';
  width: 24px;
  height: 1px;
  background: var(--teal);
}

.strapline {
  margin: 0;
  max-width: 46ch;
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  color: var(--ink-2);
  text-align: right;
}

.title {
  margin: clamp(18px, 2.6vh, 30px) 0 0;
  font-size: clamp(2.35rem, 5.6vw, 4.6rem);
  line-height: 1.02;
  letter-spacing: -0.036em;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--ink);
}

.l1,
.l2 {
  display: block;
}

.l2 {
  position: relative;
  width: fit-content;
  color: var(--teal-lit);
  padding-bottom: 16px;
}

.l2::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  bottom: 6px;
  height: 1px;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--teal), rgba(54, 190, 190, 0) 96%);
  opacity: 0.6;
}

.l2::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  bottom: 2px;
  width: 1px;
  height: 9px;
  background: var(--teal);
  opacity: 0.6;
}

.notes {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr 1.25fr;
  margin-top: clamp(26px, 4vh, 44px);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
}

.note {
  padding: 22px 32px 26px 0;
  border-right: 1px solid var(--line-2);
}

.note + .note {
  padding-left: 32px;
}

.note:last-child {
  border-right: 0;
  padding-right: 0;
}

.note__label {
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  font-family: var(--font-geist-mono);
  font-size: 10px;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-2);
}

.note__num {
  color: var(--teal);
  margin-right: 9px;
}

.note__body {
  margin: 0 0 12px;
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.62;
  color: var(--ink-2);
  max-width: 44ch;
}

.note__body:last-child {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

.note__body code {
  font-family: var(--font-geist-mono);
  font-size: 12.5px;
  color: var(--teal-lit);
  background: rgba(54, 190, 190, 0.08);
  border-radius: var(--stp-radius-small);
  padding: 1px 5px;
}

.depth {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}

.depth li {
  padding: 10px 0;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--line-2);
}

.depth li:first-child {
  border-top: 0;
  padding-top: 0;
}

.depth__k {
  display: block;
  font-family: var(--font-geist-mono);
  font-size: 9.5px;
  letter-spacing: 0.15em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-3);
  margin-bottom: 4px;
}

.depth__v {
  display: block;
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  color: var(--ink-2);
}

.cta-slot {
  margin-bottom: 16px;
}

.cta-slot :global(.cta-command) {
  display: flex;
  width: 100%;
}

.cta-slot :global(.cta-command__code) {
  font-size: 12.5px;
}

.cta-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.btn {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  height: 38px;
  padding: 0 16px;
  border-radius: var(--stp-radius-medium);
  font-size: 13.5px;
  font-weight: 550;
  line-height: 1;
  transition:
    background var(--stp-motion-duration-fast) var(--stp-motion-easing),
    border-color var(--stp-motion-duration-fast) var(--stp-motion-easing);
}

.btn--solid {
  color: var(--ink);
  background: rgba(54, 190, 190, 0.1);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(54, 190, 190, 0.34);
}

.btn--solid:hover {
  background: rgba(54, 190, 190, 0.17);
}

.btn--ghost {
  color: var(--ink-2);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line);
}

.btn--ghost:hover {
  color: var(--ink);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line-2), inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);
}

.fine {
  margin: 16px 0 0;
  font-size: 11.5px;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: var(--ink-3);
  max-width: 52ch;
}

.plate {
  margin: clamp(28px, 4.5vh, 52px) 0 0;
  border-radius: 12px;
  overflow: hidden;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.024), rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2));
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08),
    0 34px 90px -46px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.95);
}

.plate__head {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 18px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  padding: 13px 18px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2);
  font-family: var(--font-geist-mono);
  font-size: 10px;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-3);
}

.plate__head-r {
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3);
}

.plate__canvas {
  overflow-x: auto;
  padding: 12px 0 6px;
  background-image:
    linear-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.022) 1px, transparent 1px),
